      "html": "<div class=\"ds-table-wrap\"><table class=\"ds-table\"><thead><tr><th>Serie</th><th>Último dato</th><th>Variación</th><th>Caída</th><th>Periodo</th><th>Fuente</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>fake.up</td><td>671,35<br><small>USD</small></td><td class=\"ds-positive\">6,38 %</td><td>-1,22 %</td><td>2024-12-03<br>2024-12-31<br><small>21 · D</small></td><td>fake:fake.up · 77094139e5…</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
      "css": ".ds-table-wrap{overflow-x:auto}.ds-table{font-family:var(--hoard-font-sans,\"Source Sans 3\",sans-serif);width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;color:var(--hoard-text,#eceae1);font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-table th{text-align:left;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;padding:4px 8px;white-space:nowrap;color:var(--hoard-text-muted,#bebbb4);border-bottom:1px solid var(--hoard-border,#433f35)}.ds-table td{padding:4px 8px;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff0d}.ds-table small{font-size:12px;color:var(--hoard-text-muted,#bebbb4)}.ds-table .ds-positive{color:var(--hoard-success,#4a9e6d)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Existing Market workspace",
    "overview": "This is an extraction of the current implementation, not a new brand proposal. Watchlists extend the existing charcoal and gold Operate surface: saved sets, filters, actual observations and source information are arranged for repeated research work. The old Market search, comparison and series tools remain below the new panel.\n\nThe descriptive language here is inferred from the supplied implementation. There is no formal PRODUCT document or confirmed brand metaphor. Luis explicitly authorised autonomous decisions; the scoped extraction therefore does not invent one or replace the incumbent world. Tokens are normative for this documented scope; shared theme generation remains the runtime authority.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm charcoal surfaces with a single gold action accent.",
      "Compact sans text, serif page heading and tabular numbers.",
      "Named lists and original series data have separate lifecycles.",
      "Complete source information remains available in every result row."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Source Rule",
        "body": "Show the currency or unit, frequency, observation dates and source identity beside the observation; do not present rows as if they were converted into one common unit.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep saved-list membership independent of the Market selection.",
      "Do retain all result columns and source details inside the mobile table scroller.",
      "Do preserve existing snapshot data when removing a list member.",
      "Do describe saved records as persistent and active selection as explicit after reload.",
      "Do preserve partial-refresh outcomes and concurrent member edits.",
      "Do capture draft context before asynchronous lookups."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't imply the rows have a common currency, calendar frequency or converted unit.",
      "Don't calculate percentages without the positive bases required by the source.",
      "Don't treat an uncomputed metric as zero.",
      "Don't replace this existing Operate world with a new visual identity.",
      "Don't describe supplied screenshots or author receipts as tests rerun by this documenter."
    ]
  }
}
